# The old-channel thread and the injury rescue. Arc, owners and plants:
# content/STORY_BIBLE.md (spoilers). Voice: content/STYLE.md.
# Thread owners (`who ow_*`) are cast once per voyage and never overlap.

card m_carrier
type event
cat mystery
clue core
due
once
days 15 19
roles A
when !is A ow_list
when !is A ow_song
when !is A ow_garden
when !is A ow_letter
when !is A ow_dose
text {A}'s spare dish, trained on Mars for the arrival tests, still scans the old common channel, which nothing on Earth listens to. It logs a carrier too faint to lock. Folded at 10.96 seconds, 2.4 percent duty, it stands up like a fence post. "An alias," {A} says. "Something of ours."
do who ow_hail A
do mark t_carrier

card m_alias
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 18 19
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when since t_carrier >= 3
text {A} asks {B} to point a second dish at it. Ship machinery would alias differently on each ship; fleet software would keep fleet time. The bursts land on both in the same millisecond, and drift against fleet time like something with its own crystal. "Not us," {A} tells the fleet. "Ignore my last."
do bond A B 3
do open dec_signal

card dec_signal
type decision
cat mystery
days 18 19
weight 1
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious open log
when fired m_alias
when is A ow_hail
text Whatever the carrier is, it isn't the fleet's. {A} wants to answer every burst with a standard hello, blind, until someone can read what it says, and sign the reply with the old program key the fleet still carries. {B} points out that every reply ties up the comms computer, and the letters wait.
option open | Answer every burst | {A} adds one line to the comms schedule: answer every burst, standard hello, until someone says stop. The first goes out at 14:02, and {A} logs every answer to the millisecond.
  set signal_answered
  mark t_signal
  morale B -3
  trait A curious 5
option log | Log it, keep going | The carrier goes into the anomaly log under "later". {A} clips the folded trace inside the logbook, just in case, and the comms computer stays on the letters.
  set signal_ignored
  mark t_signal
  morale A -5

card signal_reply
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 28 29
roles A
when flag signal_answered
when is A ow_hail
text At 03:12 the receiver catches half a frame of housekeeping on the old channel, in a format no one flies now, cut off a byte before the field that says who sent it. The fleet's answers go out on schedule, every one. Mission Control replies eight minutes later: "say again."
do trait A curious 4

card signal_echo
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 28 31
roles A
when flag signal_ignored
when is A ow_hail
text Folding a week of noise, {A} finds half a frame of housekeeping on the old channel, in a format no one flies now, cut off a byte before the field that says who sent it. Averaged over a day, its period hasn't moved by a millisecond. The anomaly report calls it "persistent".
do morale A -3

# Injury and rescue: needs supplies from another ship.
card c_hail
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 39 39
roles A
when is A ow_hail
text {A} works out how many times the old-channel carrier has knocked since the fleet first heard it: close to half a million. Every gap has a reason, Mars in the way or a cold night, and every knock lands on the beat. "Half a million. Every gap explained. Patient. Out," {A} sends.
do trait A curious 1

card crisis_eva
type event
cat grim
once
days 10 34
weight 6
roles A
when cond A ok
when kit_elsewhere A
text During {A}'s scheduled EVA a tether snags on a bracket and wrenches {A}'s arm, with a suited crewmate watching from the next ship's hatch. {A} frees it, secures every tool, works back along the line hand over hand, and comes inside with a wrist that won't bend.
do cond A injured
do who eva_who A
do morale A -10
do open rescue_kit

card rescue_kit
type rescue
cat grim
duration 1
roles A B
default volunteer
when cond A injured
when bestbond B A
text {A} needs the ultrasound probe from another ship's medical kit, and the next scheduled transfer window is days away.
option send | Send the kit | The fleet holds formation tight for an unscheduled transfer, and the kit rides the line across alone. {A}'s wrist is scanned and splinted by lunch, and the anomaly report runs to four pages.
  kit A
  res fuel -1
  morale A 6
option volunteer | {B} brings it over | {B} rides the line across with the kit in an unscheduled window and splints the wrist personally. The mission log calls it "nominal". Six ships read the log, and every one of them knows better.
  kitfrom B A
  move B A
  res fuel -1
  bond A B 12
  morale B 4
